        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most damp basements, a 50 pint dehumidifier is the right size, and the Frigidaire FHDD5034Y1 is the one to buy if you have a floor drain or are happy to use the bucket: large bucket, three speeds, a 41°F rating and Wi-Fi at no extra cost. If you have no drain, the Frigidaire FHDP5033Y1 pump model is the better choice; for a cold basement, the Hisense AHD5024K1W's 38°F rating and two-year warranty make it the value pick.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check that the 50 pints refers to the 2019 test, discount the square footage on the box, and set the humidistat to about 50%. Sort out drainage first and the machine will do the rest.
